  "notes": "A ずる verb (literary ichidan form of {禁|きん}じる). Both {禁|きん}ずる and {禁|きん}じる are used, with {禁|きん}じる being more common in modern Japanese. The ずる form appears in signs, formal writing, and set phrases.\n\nKEY EXPRESSION:\n{禁|きん}じえない (unable to suppress/hold back) is a very common literary expression used with emotions: {涙|なみだ}を{禁|きん}じえない (unable to hold back tears), {驚|おどろ}きを{禁|きん}じえない (unable to suppress one's astonishment).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {喫煙|きつえん}を{禁|きん}ずる — to prohibit smoking\n- {法律|ほうりつ}で{禁|きん}じる — to prohibit by law\n- {涙|なみだ}を{禁|きん}じえない — unable to hold back tears\n- {驚|おどろ}きを{禁|きん}じえない — unable to suppress astonishment\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {禁止|きんし}する — to prohibit; the most common modern way to express prohibition, while {禁|きん}ずる is more literary\n- {制限|せいげん}する — to restrict; implies limiting rather than completely banning",
